e":"Add MainApp tests","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"test-code":{"insertions":300,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"7002c3a48a79fd39e450c56976fd6d958758f7eb","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Fix startup crash on null values in JSON files","messageBody":"A hand-edited data or preferences file can contain a JSON null where\nthe app expects a value. Jackson parses this without error, so the null\nreaches later code and causes a NullPointerException. MainApp only\ncatches DataLoadingException, so its fallback for invalid files is\nskipped and the app exits without opening a window. The user guide lets\nadvanced users edit the data file and says an invalid file starts the\napp with empty lists, so this breaks documented behaviour.\n\nLet\u0027s treat each of these cases as invalid data, so the existing\nfallbacks apply:\n\n* JsonUtil#readJsonFile: a file containing only null. This affects both\n  the data file and the preferences file.\n* JsonUserPrefsStorage#readUserPrefs: a null guiSettings. Jackson sets\n  the field directly, which bypasses the null check in\n  UserPrefs#setGuiSettings.\n* JsonSerializableAddressBook#toModelType: a null jobseeker or client\n  entry.\n* JsonAdaptedJobseeker#toModelType and JsonAdaptedClient#toModelType: a\n  null tag entry.\n\nNull is rejected as invalid file rather than treated as a missing file.\nUsing Optional.ofNullable in readJsonFile would make the app load the\nsample data and overwrite the user\u0027s file.\n\nAn invalid preferences file now falls back to the defaults and is\nrepaired. An invalid data file starts the app with empty lists and stays\non disk until the next command is run. MainApp itself does not change.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":29,"deletions":1},"test-code":{"insertions":161,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"5ab0f2e839f119c17df0b3a933c45fb6750f62f6","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add hash code tests","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"test-code":{"insertions":77,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"73c46549cc6df087f6f725ee0e04496db0bcffad","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add tests for four uncovered methods","messageBody":"LogicManager#setGuiSettings, StorageManager#getUserPrefsFilePath,\nUniquePersonList#iterator and ModelManager#setAddressBook are not called\nby any test. Each one only passes the call on to another object, so a\nmistake in the wiring would go unnoticed: window settings would not be\nsaved, for example, or the wrong file path would be returned.\n\nLet\u0027s add tests for these methods:\n\n* setGuiSettings: null and valid settings, checking that valid settings\n  reach the model\n* getUserPrefsFilePath: the exact path, because a non-null check would\n  still pass if the address book path were returned instead\n* iterator: lists of 0, 1 and 2 people, returned in list order\n* setAddressBook: a null book, and replacement books with no people,\n  only jobseekers, only clients, and both\n\nLet\u0027s also check that setAddressBook keeps hidden people hidden. The\nfilter set by the constructor has to apply to the new data, or replacing\nthe data would reveal those people.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"test-code":{"insertions":96,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"410e0e63d40478fbefca9b1f991077726e522c0b","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Edit test names for FindJobseekerCommandTest","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"test-code":{"insertions":7,"deletions":7}}},{"hash":"7be4018c385298e71adef63872ca0c28306409a7","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #167 from kkyingovo/branch-use-cases","messageBody":"Update Developer Guide use cases for accuracy and consistency","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"70018fa7586881afb6ae043dbdbd8f35b60c0a64","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #176 from PenguinPiplup/branch-update-find-command-tests","messageBody":"Update find command tests","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"13a0a137012cf7d1bd07e4e21efeefee5bf97cd5","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add dedicated message for null tag entries in JSON files","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":4,"deletions":2},"test-code":{"insertions":4,"deletions":4}}},{"hash":"ea6986c6b87e94e4111c464d5732f45ffb63f03c","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #182 from PenguinPiplup/branch-fix-null-json-startup-crash","messageBody":"Fix startup crash on null values in JSON files","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"675357a2589f157ed320eab731bc2b6989a1b11b","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Remove ignored ParticipantPadding setting from diagram style","messageBody":"PlantUML v1.2026.9 no longer supports `skinparam ParticipantPadding`.\nIt draws a yellow warning box into every diagram that includes\nstyle.puml, while still exiting successfully.\n\nDelete the setting rather than using the `\u003cstyle\u003e` replacement that\nthe warning suggests. The setting is already ignored, so deleting it\nkeeps the current layout, whereas the replacement makes the participant\nboxes and the diagram slightly larger.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":0,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"dc8721c41e423cf4d5022b29275806944895b2b4","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update UI section of DG","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":16,"deletions":3}}},{"hash":"cec800903069364dca188bd7cc7e2370c31fc124","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Make further refinements to DG UI section","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":9,"deletions":9}}},{"hash":"d0bbe0e55fbd165e414970d9c4ba394e171cb9ed","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Make further refinements to DG UI section","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":6,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"ab0399479895480cb73dcd2bfd926ed79ef0e270","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add help window tests to ensure working links","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"test-code":{"insertions":154,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"b4abc579376e64b0ec0bcfbfb9a6c7eeb7cc03bb","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update AboutUs.md","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":3,"deletions":12}}},{"hash":"39868a4818d6485dcbf2b916df0bf80b10f0c7e9","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Remove archiving data files section from UG","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":0,"deletions":4}}},{"hash":"378773ee12ce9dd1122474136d235095c07c0115","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #192 from vutuanlong07/tp-133-alt","messageBody":"Fix more typos and missing sections","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-11-02T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"39d0b4c96d9d684b6e516101f2ca1ac34bddf12d","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Fix factual inaccuracies for find commands","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":5,"deletions":4}}},{"hash":"0994cfed74d57bbce61a21bb871f5b7f76798f45","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update contacts common info","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":13,"deletions":6}}},{"hash":"698876d8f31f91b0d6efba2548d12360500a7fc9","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update inaccuracy in editj in UG","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":1,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"ab000f2e80efbe75d6bbeebd2713790e3b80d02d","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Fix inaccuracies in UG for manual file edits","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":11,"deletions":8}}},{"hash":"845eda93a14933a8e3b7e342463f64c61ab1bd82","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #189 from PenguinPiplup/branch-update-dg-ui-section","messageBody":"Update UI component in DG","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"69c3aa61cd3f57cbd085fbb1a55e0b50f3b75346","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update User Guide","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":21,"deletions":15}}},{"hash":"d306b2c8338d7b203113196db05edc24db386bd4","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #195 from plainxjane/branch-fixAutocomplete","messageBody":"Fix disappearing suggestions in command autocomplete","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"515d10a4bd4f08815e862262bf3e19512f744fa4","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #196 from PenguinPiplup/branch-update-ug","messageBody":"Fix factual errors in UG/Update User Guide","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"290a48ab91a47718fe9a7c207919abcc8b8099b0","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Allow \u0027/\u0027 in person names such as s/o and d/o","messageBody":"Previously, valid names such as \"Raj s/o Kumar\" were rejected because\nName\u0027s regex banned \u0027/\u0027 outright, on the reasoning that it is reserved\nfor command prefixes. That ban is wider than the parser needs.\nArgumentTokenizer only splits on its known prefixes when a space comes\nbefore them, so \"s/o\" and \"d/o\" already reach Name intact, and only\nthe regex stopped them.\n\nChange Name.VALIDATION_REGEX to \"[^\\s].*\", the same as Address, so that\na name is invalid only if it is blank or starts with whitespace. Clients\nshare Name, so their names benefit too, e.g. \"ABC / XYZ Holdings\".\n\nTwo other options were considered but rejected:\n* Allowing only s/o, d/o and similar words. The same bug would return\n  for the next name that is missing from the list. (such as Maersk A/S)\n* Escape syntax (a\\/l): this is the only option that fully solves a/l,\n  but it makes users learn new syntax. Additionally, it can be more\n  troublesome if the recruiter copy pastes common names such as \"s/o\"\n  and \"d/o\" from somewhere else, and the recruiter has to add the\n  escape syntax manually.\n\nThis has two known limitations:\n* A mistyped prefix can now be saved as part of a name, e.g.\n  \"editj 1 n/John P/123\" renames the person to \"John P/123\".\n* A lowercase word that starts with a prefix, such as \"a/l\", \"p/l\" or\n  \"t/a\", is still read as that prefix. An escape syntax would solve this\n  but would change the tokenizer during the feature freeze. Prefixes are\n  case-sensitive, so the user guide now tells users to write these words\n  in capitals.\n\nTest data that used a \u0027/\u0027 to mean an invalid name is now valid, so it\nuses a blank name or a leading space instead. New parser tests cover\nnames containing \u0027/\u0027 and record how the lowercase words above are read.\n\nFixes #180\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":5,"deletions":4},"docs":{"insertions":4,"deletions":2},"test-code":{"insertions":125,"deletions":15}}},{"hash":"7f18b3292cf02d911f9eb7b369c9f15863325aa0","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update DG for find commands","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":219,"deletions":7}}},{"hash":"af0b232399bae8765b8175ab68f16bd2cffba583","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Fix stale filter claim in DG Edit section","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":3,"deletions":5}}},{"hash":"7d94a26a655e3040f275d208a56c151481c01a5e","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #197 from PenguinPiplup/branch-fix-name-slash","messageBody":"Allow \u0027/\u0027 in person names such as s/o and d/o","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"86fcc8c48929f24e338a62c244469cfd68fe2004","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #201 from plainxjane/branch-updateSampleData","messageBody":"Update sample data","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"60e5c9babf5f2a937afa632d8ff84eabd5588ef1","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Make changes to findcommand UML diagrams","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":28,"deletions":18}}},{"hash":"fa04170f6955167d21a5909a26a2c853bd3bd096","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Simplify FindJobseekerSequenceDiag